WEBVTT

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.580
It's a woman...

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.120
Whoa!

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:33.950
Are you okay?! Hey!

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.450
She's very weak.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.660
Call Quitterie!

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.660
Got it!

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.370
Ulgar, get us the anti-gravity cart.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.000
--Let's get her back to our ship!
--Yeah.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.120
Is this... a dream?

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.290
Hey, can you hear me?

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.580
Who... are you? What happened to me?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.830
You were asleep in a hibernation pod.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.330
Hibernation...

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:57.660
Welcome back.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:09.540
Oh... Help is here... I can go home...

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.660
Go back... to Earth.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:23.700
Um... Everyone, thank you so much.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.000
I'm still a bit confused, but...

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.540
We understand. Don't push yourself.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.410
You've been asleep for a very long time.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:36.290
There's some risk of memory damage that
concerns me. Do you remember who you are?

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:42.250
Yes. I'm okay. I am an astronaut.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:46.830
Polina Livinskaya,
crew member of the <i>Ark VI</i>.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:19.500
"Planet Icriss
Polina's recollection"

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:24.580
"Planet Icriss
Polina's recollection"
We were on our way to a different planet,
but needed to make an emergency landing

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:28.910
"Planet Icriss
Polina's recollection"
on this planet due to malfunctions
in the ship and our communicator.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.910
We were attacked by plants...

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.870
Crash-landed under that cliff...

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:41.410
And the other crew members who went
outside never came back.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.830
I was all alone,
and there was nothing I could do.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:51.870
So I entered the hibernation device,
betting on whatever slim hope I had.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.750
By the way,

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.830
what was the purpose of your ship?

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:06.620
I'm sorry, I'm still a little dizzy
and my memory isn't all there.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.620
It's like a bad hangover.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:11.500
Oh, don't worry, take your time.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.040
It's refreshing, having an adult lady on board...

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.950
What's the deal with you?

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:20.410
Ah, yes... Investigation.
Planetary investigation.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:24.160
We were on a mission to find planets
suited for human habitation.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.870
You were on a Type Ark ship like mine.
Did you have a different mission?

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:34.200
Well... We're not really on a mission,
to be exact...

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.660
We kind of found this ship.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:39.500
Found it?! What? How?!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.120
Oh, sorry, I said it like I found a bike
in an empty lot.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.290
But we really did just find it.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:47.500
Where?!

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.120
In space.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.500
In space?!

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.910
Are you all idiots?! You're confusing her!
Don't give her all the details at once!

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:59.540
Yeah, let's discuss the ball of light from
camp sending us 5,000 light years away

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.080
on a different occasion.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.660
What? What are you saying?!

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.830
She just said don't confuse her!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.160
I haven't laughed in such a long time..

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.450
I am really glad.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:20.080
I had all but given up, but...
I'm really going to get home...

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:27.500
Polina, there's actually something
we need to tell you.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:33.790
This ship is also broken.
We're stranded here as well.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:38.330
We got lost, and we were
on our way home on this ship.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:42.500
We landed on this planet to get food,
but we got in an accident...

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:46.410
Our reactor is broken.
This ship can't get to space.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.540
No...

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.000
Polina!

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.160
Let me see her!

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.040
She's okay, just asleep.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:06.200
It's only natural. She was asleep for 12 years.
She needs more time to recover.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:12.540
It really is quite a miracle, though,
finding her ship on this huge planet.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.910
Not really.

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:19.870
Only the central belt area of this planet
is habitable for life.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:25.580
If we narrow it down to areas that have
those carnivorous plants...

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:30.120
The two ships crashing close to each other
isn't as unlikely as it might seem.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:34.290
Hmph. Two ships of the same type,
both broken near each other.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.790
It's like two coffins side by side.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:39.200
Why does this guy have to say stuff like that?

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.080
This guy wants attention.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.910
What?!

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:44.750
Zack.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.160
Can you pass me your snack?

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.040
What?!

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.370
Why now? That's very greedy of you Aries!
This is mine!

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:54.330
Oh, no! I just want to borrow it!

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.290
This ship can split up into sections, right?

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.450
Yeah.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:05.660
As an emergency measure, the ship can
separate into three blocks.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:08.500
Not a feature we would normally use, but...

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:13.160
Polina's <i>Ark VI </i>was damaged in the central
residential block, and the reactor was not.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:18.290
Meanwhile, our <i>Astra </i>is only damaged
in the reactor section.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:23.080
So if we take this, bring it here...

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.330
That's right!

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:27.700
We can connect the functional blocks together...

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.660
...and fix the ship!

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.790
How is it, Zack?!

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:01.450
We've managed to connect.
I think this is working.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:03.160
Good!

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.620
We're going home.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.410
Yeah.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:12.370
To be honest, I was hit pretty hard
by the fact that I crashed our ship.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:15.000
We've been through some
bad things on this trip,

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:19.120
but now that we see hope, I'm starting
to feel like this trip isn't so bad.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:24.500
When we get home safely,
I'm getting my own ship.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.830
Then I'm off to space again.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:29.500
You said you would be my pilot, right?

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:34.750
If you get a ship, yeah. How many years
is that going to take?

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:36.750
Like, seven years maybe?

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:41.580
Nobody can get a ship at 24 years old! Get real.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:48.290
Oh, great. The ship blocks' connections
are working out?

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:51.120
Yes! I'm very glad.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:55.080
I am starting to not feel too bad about
how exciting this trip is, but...

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.160
...I'd like to go back to life in peace, too.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:01.700
Peace, yes...

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.500
Oh, I forgot to ask an important question.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:08.700
What year is it now?

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:12.120
Right now, it's September, 2063 A.D.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.080
You've been asleep for 12 years.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:16.700
Twelve years?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:24.370
2063?! Did you say 2063?!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.290
Polina?!

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.700
What does that mean?

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.410
Nothing happened?

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.410
What are you talking about?

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.540
Nothing happened...?

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.040
What's wrong, Polina?

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.620
I'm sorry. It's nothing.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:50.200
I'm still... confused.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:55.950
I'll come by later to check in.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.450
Thank you...

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.370
Lord...

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.250
“Planet Icriss
Day 80 of being lost in space”

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:13.950
My friends.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:18.910
Thanks to the hard work of our own Zack,
and our new friend Polina,

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:21.450
the ship docking procedure is a success!

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:23.870
Yay!

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:26.410
We're going home... Home.

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:30.120
This time I really thought it was over.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:36.200
I never gave up. Survival tip number five:
when you give up, it's game over.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.620
You totally did give up.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:43.250
For a crew of only children to come so far...

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:48.450
This positive atmosphere
must have helped them greatly.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:54.950
I have an update regarding the food search.

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:56.660
Astounding.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:11:00.450
The plants on this planet have an organ
similar to an animal heart.

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:03.080
Some species can even move, though slowly.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.450
It's like they're animals!

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:10.330
It's like me. Boundaries don't
have to be so clear-cut.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.870
Male or female. Animal or plant.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.330
Comedy anime and sci-fi anime.

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:16.950
What did you say?

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:18.080
Anyway.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.160
Anyway?!

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:23.750
I've confirmed that several
of the moving plants are edible.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:27.620
There's a little trick to harvesting them...

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.950
Gross!

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.700
Since they're basically plants, if you
block their photosynthesis, they stop.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.870
Just like Charce said.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:57.290
I'll hunt these types.
You go and collect the harmless ones.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:59.000
Okay.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.620
But take a break first.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:02.160
Here, mushroom tea.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.040
Have some biscuits, too.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:11.540
Everyone's working hard to get off
this planet as soon as possible.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:14.540
We need to give it one more push.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:17.160
Yeah.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:21.370
Remember how you asked me
to live together with you?

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.330
Because I do.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.580
What did you mean by that?

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:29.200
Huh?

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:35.450
I meant what I said. If the ship won't fly,
we all have to live here together.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:38.250
You insensitive, useless mass of muscle
with glasses!

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:46.410
But I'm really glad the ship is fixed...

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:50.160
If we had to live here, there wouldn't be
any use for dreams and aspirations.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:54.370
Your dream. To become a doctor?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.160
Not just that.

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.250
How about you? Don't you want to join
your dad in research?

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:05.290
I thought he was really famous,
doing something ground-breaking.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:11.830
Memory transplant. He got close,
but there's a big hurdle he needs to clear.

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:15.410
You don't really like your father, right?

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:19.580
Similar to my mom.
Single parent, super busy...

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:22.290
Never has time for the kids.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:28.620
That by itself wasn't a problem,
since I enjoy being alone, but...

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.750
My face? Did you draw this in school?

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:57.450
Some parents don't like their kids.
It's not the end of the world.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.160
But...

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:03.700
Those eyes. It's like he was
looking at a doll.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.950
Dry, emotionless, like marbles made of glass.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:13.500
His research changed him.
I don't want to become like him.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:17.540
I want to get into research in outer space.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.830
I want to study, get back out into space,

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:24.000
and see things I've never seen before.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:29.290
I already have a captain candidate.
I promised to get on Kanata's ship.

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:32.040
That's my dream.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:38.200
I envy you boys. Just always moving forward.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:41.080
I wish my real dream could come true.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.660
Real dream? Why? You should pursue it, too.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.040
Leave it alone.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:48.700
Becoming a doctor was just something
your mother wanted you to do.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.200
If you have your own dream, I support you.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:55.450
Survival tip number five:
if you give up, it's game over.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.750
It's impossible, you idiot!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.330
You don't know how I feel,
always talking about yourself!

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.620
That's why it's obvious to me
that it won't come true!

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:06.910
My real dream is...

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:11.540
...to become your wife!

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:14.580
Huh?

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:19.250
That again...

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:20.830
We're...

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:22.290
...getting married, right?

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:23.790
Huh?!

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.410
M... M...

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:28.790
Married?! What in the world are you saying?!

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.120
--Um...
--Are you an idiot?!

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.870
--But...
--Are you out of your mind?!

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:34.160
But we promised.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:36.620
May of 2052.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.200
Marry me.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:43.080
Okay.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:46.580
But... we were kids.

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:49.950
People tend to just pretend
those things never happened.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.540
Really?

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:54.450
I've always been in love with you.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:16:01.450
Enough is enough! You have no right
to criticize your dad's emotionless eyes!

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.580
Team B5, camp log.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:08.410
Today, Zack and Quitterie
promised to marry each other.

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:14.330
“Planet Icriss
Day 87 of being lost in space”

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:19.120
“Planet Icriss
Day 87 of being lost in space”
I'm sorry. I'm sure you wanted to leave
right away, since we're ready.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:22.000
It really pains me to make
such a selfish request.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:27.290
No, don't mention it. We have to check
before we leave this planet.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.790
The place where my crewmates lost contact...

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:34.580
I knew the location,
but never actually went there.

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:40.870
It was a good decision. Going to such
a place unarmed is like a death wish.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.370
That thought crossed my mind, to be honest.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:47.540
To perish there and become part
of this planet with my friends.

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:48.790
But...

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:53.950
You decided to live and go into hibernation.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.580
I respect you for that.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:02.700
Let's let them know that you're
leaving this place alive.

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:12.500
Were they really here?
It's just an empty, barren plain.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:16.500
If Polina's memories are accurate,
this should be the place.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:18.370
How are you feeling?

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:22.540
It feels good to be outside.
It's been a long time.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:25.950
Polina, over here!

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.540
Is that it?

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:40.830
That's it. That's the <i>Ark VI </i>rover.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:44.160
So this is where...

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.870
I don't see any signs of trouble, though.

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:55.790
Why is it flipped over, anyway?

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:59.160
It's really bumpy around here,
hard to walk.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:03.660
What's this?

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:07.750
An ID Tag!

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.160
It's Glen's!

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:20.200
Everyone, get away from this place!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.330
Whoa!

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:26.910
They were hiding underground!

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.200
Whoa!

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.500
Run!

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.540
They'll attack if you stay too close!

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.660
Is this for real?!

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:43.040
Polina, what are you doing?!
We have to run!

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:51.330
I've got this. You go ahead.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.370
But--!

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:53.250
Hurry!

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.620
She's all yours, Ulgar.

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:59.290
That thing is important to our big sister.

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:02.540
I'm taking it back, you big bamboo shoot.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:08.660
What is he doing?

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:12.950
He was raised as a decathlete
from a very young age.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.870
In other words, he was born
to be a king of athletes!

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:22.500
I'll take that now.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:24.750
Whoa?!

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:26.410
I'm taking off now!

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:37.000
Thank you Kanata, truly...

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:42.200
And thank you, too. If you hadn't noticed
right away, it might have gotten us.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:45.950
When I saw the car flipped over,
I thought maybe that was why.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:48.700
I guess my friends told me.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.910
I'm glad you were able to at least have
one thing to remember them by.

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:53.370
Yes.

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:56.700
Now I'm ready to leave this place.

00:19:56.700 --> 00:20:03.790
Glenn, Dima, Phillip, Bart, I'm sorry
I couldn't mark your graves.

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:06.790
But I will serve as living proof for all of you.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:13.700
Team B5, camp log.
Day 87 of being lost in space.

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:19.750
After a long 11-day stay, we were finally
able to leave Planet Icriss.

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:25.040
The <i>Astra </i>is now on its way to the final planet.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:27.950
Oh yeah, all fixed up.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:29.290
My anti-gravity shoes.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:31.370
Oh, it was broken.

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:35.910
Yeah, there were some parts on
the <i>Ark VI </i>that Zack used to fix them.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:41.450
Hey, everyone! Charce baked a special cake
made from Icriss ingredients!

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:42.290
Wow!

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:43.370
Yay!

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:47.330
Ouch!

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:48.540
Ack!

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:50.370
Hey!

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.370
Are you okay...?

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.700
Oh, I'm so hungry. Did...

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:58.410
--Did something idiotic happen
to make this mess?!

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:01.580
--Mmm, delicious...
--Did something idiotic happen
to make this mess?!

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:04.250
Looking forward to the last planet!

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:08.160
Let's have a party!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.290
Party?

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:13.580
The "Congratulations we left Planet Icriss
and welcome Polina to the team" party!

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.000
Too long!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:21.660
Ship maintenance is finished, but that
last incident was only a short while ago.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:23.200
Polina, will you be okay?

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:27.910
I'm fine now. I'm very grateful
for your consideration.

00:21:27.910 --> 00:21:30.250
I haven't had a party in so long.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:33.120
What's wrong, Quitterie?

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.580
Hmm? Oh, sorry, I wasn't listening.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:37.040
Is something wrong?

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:43.870
It's weird. When we donated blood for Polina,
I checked everyone's blood types.

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:46.790
Funi and I have the same blood type.

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:48.500
Oh! It's the same!

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:51.620
That can't be very rare.

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:55.000
There's more to blood types
than the ABO system.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:22:01.080
There's like the MN and the P. It's close
to impossible to have a complete match.

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.950
What do you mean? Isn't it just because
you two are sisters?

00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:07.120
We aren't real siblings.

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:11.830
Funi's mother was my mom's best friend.
When she passed away, my mom adopted her.

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:16.410
I see. I thought you two were real sisters.

00:22:16.410 --> 00:22:19.250
You two are so alike.

00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:26.200
It's true, they look alike.
So maybe they could actually be sisters.

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:28.950
I wouldn't be surprised if my mom
did something like that.

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:33.250
A hidden child she left with a friend
for some reason...

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:39.120
Let's look into this. We can use
the ship's computer to compare DNAs.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.290
Right.

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:42.660
Right!

00:22:42.660 --> 00:22:44.790
Why not? Let's check it out.

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:48.500
This is getting interesting.

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:54.790
But what would I do if Funi
was my real sister...?

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:56.790
I just might love her too much.

00:23:05.290 --> 00:23:09.370
What is this...? What does this mean?

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:11.580
Could it be...?

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:13.450
Yes.

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:15.450
So that's it...

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:21.830
Why are you telling me?

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:25.290
I thought you should know first.

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:30.000
Even though the results are for
Quitterie and Funi? Well, okay.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:35.580
I have the results. As we suspected,
Quitterie and Funi aren't unrelated.

00:23:39.790 --> 00:23:41.830
They're the same person.
